message.content:
{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on SUVARNA KARNATAKA completed projects undertaken by KHB across Karnataka from 2009 to 2018. It supports tracking of housing initiatives and helps users review project completion over the stated period for planning, monitoring, and policy analysis. The focus on completed works makes it useful for stakeholders assessing outcomes of housing programmes in Karnataka under the SUVARNA KARNATAKA initiative.",
  "generated_sector": "Housing; Urban Housing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Sahitya Academy supports multi-year programs in Karnataka that promote literature and related art forms. The catalog brings together information on program types and functions, along with beneficiary coverage and the places where activities are conducted. It is useful for tracking how literary initiatives are planned and delivered, and for understanding the target audiences and scope of cultural outreach within Karnataka.",
  "generated_sector": "Art and Culture; Literature"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides district-wise Sakala applications statistics for Karnataka, covering month-wise counts of applications received, approved, rejected, and disposed. It supports monitoring and performance assessment of service delivery workflows, enabling comparisons across districts and time periods. The focus on application lifecycle outcomes makes it useful for governance reporting, operational review, and identifying bottlenecks in approvals and disposals. Data is organized to reflect administrative processing status at the district level.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; District Adminstration"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on the sale of cotton khadi in Punjab, covering trade activity across wholesale and retail channels. It supports analysis of market participation and sales patterns for khadi products made from cotton, useful for monitoring demand and distribution. The datasets are intended to help stakeholders and researchers understand the local khadi sales ecosystem within Punjab’s market context.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Agricultural Produces"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sale of electricity by use categories in Punjab, including domestic, commercial, industrial, public lighting (bulk and other), and agriculture. It supports analysis of electricity consumption and demand patterns across major consumer segments, useful for planning, monitoring, and policy decisions in the power sector. The data is organized to compare sales across these uses within Punjab over the catalog’s coverage period.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers data on the sale of electricity per consumer for the Domestic sector in Punjab. It supports analysis of electricity consumption and billing patterns at the consumer level, helping stakeholders understand demand dynamics and inform planning and policy decisions in the power sector. The focus on domestic consumers makes it useful for benchmarking, trend assessment, and service delivery monitoring within Punjab’s electricity distribution context.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers data on the sale of power across multiple consumer categories, including domestic, commercial, industrial, agricultural, public lighting, and bulk supply. It supports analysis of electricity demand patterns by sector and can be used for planning, monitoring, and policy review related to power distribution and consumption. The geographic coverage is Punjab, focusing on sector-wise power sales within the state. The underlying resources align with power and energy reporting needs.",
  "generated_sector": "Power and Energy; Renewable"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Samagra Shiksha Abhiyan (SSA), Tamil Nadu catalog compiles statistics on schools, students, and teachers under the SSA initiative. It supports monitoring of education access and staffing patterns, enabling planning and review of secondary education delivery in Tamil Nadu. The focus is on the City of Statistics on Schools, Students and Teachers within Tamil Nadu, helping stakeholders analyze program coverage and trends for school-level stakeholders.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers sanctions of funds under the Matching Grant Scheme for the Muslim Women Aid Society in Tamil Nadu from 2014-15 to 2018-19. It focuses on minority-focused women’s support through grant-based assistance, enabling tracking of funding decisions across the specified financial years. The information is useful for monitoring scheme implementation, verifying grant allocations, and supporting program review and accountability for social development initiatives in Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Minority"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together district-wise annual reporting on sanctioned loans for Maharashtra. It supports analysis of loan sanction trends over time at the district level, helping stakeholders compare uptake across regions and identify areas with higher or lower credit flow. The focus on sanctioned loans makes it useful for planning, monitoring, and policy review related to industrial and economic financing within Maharashtra.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Manufacturing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles the sanctioned strength of civil police in Punjab by category as on 31st March. It covers category-wise sanctioned posts across ranks such as director generals, senior superintendents, inspector generals, sub inspectors, head constables, and mounted constables. The information supports police administration planning, staffing assessment, and policy monitoring for law enforcement capacity at the state level. Data is published under the Home Affairs and Enforcement domain.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Enforcement Organizations"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Sanjeevini KSLPS Key Performance Indicator catalog compiles Key Performance Indicators for Sanjeevini KSRLPS, supporting monitoring and performance assessment of rural livelihoods initiatives. It focuses on outcomes linked to NRLM-aligned programming and community institutions such as SHGs, under the SRLM framework. The indicators help programme managers and stakeholders track progress, identify gaps, and improve implementation. Coverage is for Karnataka, reflecting state-level rural development and SHG ecosystem performance.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Scheme Wise Expenditure Details provides scheme-level expenditure information in lakhs for Karnataka, supporting analysis of how funds are allocated and utilized across watershed development and related soil and water conservation initiatives. The catalog helps track spending patterns by scheme, enabling monitoring, budgeting review, and performance assessment for water-focused development programmes. It is useful for government planners, researchers, and civil society stakeholders seeking evidence on expenditure trends at the scheme level within Karnataka.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Soil and Water Conservation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides scheme- and blockwise information on Aadhaar seeding status for beneficiaries under the Ramai Shabari Adim Pardhi Scheme. It focuses on tracking Aadhaar linkage progress across rural housing-related beneficiary records, supporting monitoring of enrolment and service delivery. The data is organized at the block level, enabling comparisons within rural areas for program review and targeted follow-up by the implementing authorities.",
  "generated_sector": "Housing; Rural Housing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Scheme for Promotion of Culture of Science (SPOCS) catalog brings together information on grants awarded to promote scientific temper and innovation. Published by the Ministry of Culture, the datasets support tracking of funding under SPOCS and can be used to study how science communication and culture of science initiatives are enabled across India. The coverage spans grant-related records for activities funded through the scheme, reflecting the scheme’s focus on encouraging scientific thinking and creativity.",
  "generated_sector": "Art and Culture; Heritage"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles scheme-wise financial and physical progress for the Supplementary Nutrition Programme in Punjab. It tracks expenditure and beneficiary coverage, including scheduled caste and non scheduled caste groups, alongside physical progress indicators related to provision of nutritious diet for children and pregnant women. The data supports monitoring and evaluation of programme implementation, budgeting, and outreach performance at the scheme level within Punjab. It is published by the concerned state programme administration for use in planning and review.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides scheme-wise loan disbursement details by the Tamil Nadu Minorities Economic Development Corporation Limited (TAMCO) across districts in Tamil Nadu. It supports analysis of TAMCO scheme performance through indicators such as loan amounts disbursed under different schemes. These district-level records are useful for monitoring minority-focused financial assistance, planning program improvements, and conducting policy and impact studies. The data is published for use by stakeholders interested in social development and minority welfare initiatives in Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Minority"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together scheme-wise performance details for the Ulemas and Other Employees Welfare Board in Tamil Nadu, focusing on physical and financial performance indicators. It supports monitoring of welfare scheme implementation and evaluation of outcomes for beneficiaries associated with the board’s mandate. The materials are useful for program management, compliance review, and policy analysis by stakeholders seeking evidence on scheme delivery within Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Minority"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles schemewise financial and physical progress data for Punjab, covering expenditure and beneficiary coverage across social welfare schemes. It tracks the number of beneficiaries by scheduled caste and non scheduled caste, disaggregated by male and female, and supports monitoring of scheme delivery outcomes. The indicators align with themes such as financial assistance and welfare coverage for groups including old age pensioners, widow and destitute women, dependent children, and other beneficiaries. Use cases include program review, performance monitoring, and planning at the state level.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together scholarship data for the Navi Mumbai Municipal Corporation, supporting analysis of scholarship schemes and related beneficiaries. It is useful for planning, monitoring and evaluating scholarship coverage, uptake and distribution patterns within the municipal area. The focus on scholarships enables stakeholders to assess equity and outreach of education support initiatives administered or tracked by the civic body. The geographic coverage is Navi Mumbai Municipal Corporation, with the temporal span covered by the included records.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Scholarship Details catalog provides year-wise, district-wise information on scholarships, supporting analysis of coverage, distribution, and trends over time. It is useful for education administrators, researchers, and policy makers who need to compare scholarship allocation and uptake across districts for planning and monitoring. The catalog focuses on sub-state granularity at the district level and spans multiple years as reflected by the year-wise organization. It is aligned to the broader education and welfare needs around scholarship delivery.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Adult Education"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together scholarship-related information under Sainik Welfare, focusing on scholarship details paid to the wards of ex-servicemen. It supports beneficiaries, administrators, and researchers in understanding eligibility-linked scholarship disbursement and related particulars for informed planning and verification. The scope covers scholarship information for India, reflecting nationwide applicability of the welfare scheme.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Enforcement Organizations"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on schools in Sikkim classified by management and category. It supports education planning and policy analysis by enabling comparisons across different types of school governance and institutional categories. The focus on school-level classification helps stakeholders identify coverage patterns and inform decisions related to access, resource allocation, and monitoring of education services in Sikkim.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides category-wise information on schools in Sikkim, covering school locations (urban or rural) and school levels such as Lower Primary School, Primary School, Junior High School, Secondary School, Senior Secondary School, along with Monastic School, Sanskrit School and Islamic School. It also classifies schools by management type including State Government, Central Government, Private (Aided), Private (Unaided) and Local Body School. The data supports planning and analysis of educational access and distribution across different school categories in Sikkim.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together school data for Maharashtra, covering information on schools across the state. Published by the School Education and Sports Department, Maharashtra, through the Commissionerate of Education, it supports planning, monitoring, and policy decisions for secondary education. The resources are useful for education administrators, researchers, and analysts seeking state-level insights into school-related indicators and records for Maharashtra.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "District-wise school information for Karnataka, covering counts of schools across management types, medium of instruction, and area. The catalog supports analysis of school distribution and planning needs for elementary and secondary education, including comparisons by district and management. It is useful for education administrators, researchers, and policymakers seeking to understand how school availability varies within the state. Data are organized to reflect district-level granularity and multiple classification dimensions such as management and medium.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary, Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides school-level details for Sikkim, supporting identification and verification of educational institutions across administrative and academic attributes. It covers key fields such as establishment and DISE codes, school level, management and locality information, and connectivity details including phone, email, and website. Additional location and governance linkages—district, blocks, constituencies, civic bodies, wards, and rural/urban status—help users map schools to their operational context for planning, reporting, and analysis.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The School Facility Details catalog provides information on school infrastructure and amenities in Sikkim. It covers establishment identifiers and names along with facility availability indicators such as libraries, fire extinguishing arrangements, and staff rooms. The catalog also includes counts for resources like available books and extinguisher units, supporting assessments of readiness and basic facilities across schools. It is useful for education planning, monitoring, and targeted improvements in school infrastructure within Sikkim.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together records of physical achievements under the School Health Programme during the period 2010-2015 in Tamil Nadu. It focuses on measurable outcomes related to school health activities, supporting monitoring and review of programme implementation. The information can be used by education and health stakeholders to assess progress, identify gaps, and plan improvements for future school health initiatives.",
  "generated_sector": "Health and Family welfare; Health"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers school infrastructure details for Sikkim, including school buildings and essential facilities such as toilets, water tanks, electricity, hostels, perimeter fencing, playgrounds, and indoor facilities. It supports planning and monitoring of education infrastructure needs, enabling stakeholders to assess availability of key amenities at schools. The focus on physical and utility components makes it useful for infrastructure audits, gap analysis, and targeted improvements in school facilities across Sikkim.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "A curated schools list for Sikkim that brings together school-level information such as school category, along with school names and addresses. It supports quick identification of schools for administrative planning, education outreach, and local reference use cases. The catalog is focused on education infrastructure mapping within Sikkim, enabling users to locate and compare schools by level and category using address details.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Elementary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on schools covered under the National Green Corps Programme in Punjab, along with associated capacity-building details. It tracks the number of schools reached and the training of teachers and master trainers under the programme. The data supports monitoring and evaluation of programme outreach and training outcomes for environmental education activities in Punjab.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Ecology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on schools with tap water supply under the Jal Jeevan Mission in Karnataka. It supports monitoring of water access in educational institutions and helps planners and local administrators track progress of rural water supply initiatives. The focus is on school-level tap connections and related Jal Jeevan Mission implementation under the Rural Development and Panchayati Raj framework.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Season Wise Rainfall occurred by Districts in Tamil Nadu: SCR brings together district-level rainfall information for the 2016-17, 2017-18 and 2018-19 editions. It supports analysis of seasonal rainfall patterns relevant to crop planning and agricultural decision-making. The catalog is published as part of the Statistics domain and is useful for researchers, planners and stakeholders tracking monsoon and seasonal variability across Tamil Nadu at district granularity.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides sector-wise employment statistics for Madhya Pradesh, capturing the number of employments across different sectors. It supports analysis of workforce distribution by sector and helps in planning, monitoring, and policy discussions related to employment generation and labour market trends. The focus is on employment counts within the state, enabling comparisons across sectors for stakeholders such as researchers, administrators, and analysts.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Employment"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides sector-wise information on student enrolment for the month of Dec-2021 at the Karnataka German Technical Training Institute (KGTTI). It supports analysis of enrolment distribution across education sectors within Karnataka, helping stakeholders assess participation trends and planning needs for technical training capacity. The focus is on a single monthly reference period in 2021 and the institute’s intake in Karnataka.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles selected economic indicators for Punjab (Rural Area), covering demographic composition, literacy, caste and work participation, and key agricultural performance measures. It includes indicators such as density of population, shares of literates and schedule castes, workers and agricultural workers, area sown, cropping intensity, irrigation coverage, and tractor availability. These datasets support rural socio-economic analysis and planning, including studies of livelihoods, agriculture productivity, and resource use in Punjab’s rural areas.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together selected indicators for Madhya Pradesh and India, covering demographic measures such as population, sex, literacy, birth rate, death rate, and infant mortality rate. It also includes quantifiable economic and financial indicators like per capita measures and banking-related credit and deposit ratios. These indicators support comparative analysis across Madhya Pradesh and India for planning, monitoring, and research use cases where demographic and financial context are needed.",
  "generated_sector": "Economy; Macro Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together selected information on large and medium industries in Punjab, covering key industrial performance and capacity indicators. It includes data on the number of units, fixed capital, number of employees, and production, enabling analysis of industrial scale, investment, workforce size, and output trends. These indicators support planning, monitoring, and research by stakeholders interested in industrial development within Punjab.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Manufacturing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together selected information on working small scale industries in Punjab, covering key economic indicators such as number of units, fixed capital, number of employees, and production. These measures support analysis of industrial capacity, employment levels, and output trends for small-scale enterprises. The compilation is useful for researchers, planners, and policymakers assessing the performance and scale of small industries within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Industries; Small Scale"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles statistics on semi government employees working in different enterprises in Punjab, covering multiple categories such as corporations, boards, municipal committees, improvement trusts, market committees, zila parishads and panchayat samities. It supports analysis of workforce distribution across these semi-government bodies and can be used for planning, monitoring staffing patterns, and related labour and employment studies. The focus is on Punjab, as indicated in the catalog title.",
  "generated_sector": "Labour and Employment; Employment"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Senior Fellowship Scheme Data catalog brings together information on the Senior Fellowship Scheme administered by the Ministry of Culture. It covers beneficiary and fellowship category details, fellowship amounts disbursed, and scheme status, supporting monitoring of cultural support and program performance. The data is focused on India and is useful for researchers, policymakers, and program administrators tracking uptake, funding patterns, and outcomes across fellowship categories.",
  "generated_sector": "Art and Culture; Heritage"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Senior/Young Artist Scheme catalog brings together information on financial support provided to encourage artists across cultural fields. It supports fellowships and related assistance for senior and young artists, helping sustain creative work and talent development. Published by the Ministry of Culture, the resources are focused on India and are useful for applicants, researchers, and program administrators tracking scheme benefits and eligibility-related information.",
  "generated_sector": "Art and Culture; Heritage"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers services delivered through Common Services Centres (CSCs) in Tamil Nadu, supporting citizen access to government and other essential services at the local level. It brings together information on the range of CSC offerings, helping users understand what can be availed through these service points. The focus is on improving last-mile service delivery and enabling easier uptake of public services for residents in Tamil Nadu.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Local Government"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Settlement catalog focuses on data related to settlement areas in Karnataka, supporting analysis of where and how human habitation is distributed. It is aligned with Census and Surveys activities, enabling use cases such as planning, demographic and spatial studies, and evidence-based policy discussions around settlement patterns. The catalog’s resources help researchers and administrators work with settlement-related indicators for Karnataka.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together short term skill training admission details for 2017 to 2021, supporting analysis of intake trends and applicant participation across training cycles. It is useful for planning capacity, monitoring admissions over time, and informing policy and program management for vocational skill development. The focus is on admissions data for short term courses, covering the period named in the catalog title: 2017 to 2021.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on short-term training programs offered in Government of Maharashtra Industrial Training Institutes (ITIs). It covers course names, the specific ITIs delivering the training, and training locations within Maharashtra. The collection supports planning, analysis, and awareness of state-level skill development initiatives, helping stakeholders understand available short-duration technical learning opportunities across the ITI network.",
  "generated_sector": "Education; Secondary"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Silk Data compiles information on silk plantation, production, and trade, covering imports and exports for India. It supports analysis of the silk value chain—from cultivation to market flows—useful for policy planning, industry monitoring, and research by stakeholders in the textiles sector. Published by the Ministry of Textiles, the catalog helps users track trends in silk supply and international movement of silk-related goods across the country.",
  "generated_sector": "Textiles; Sericulture"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers the Right to Service (RTS) application report for Sindhudurg, tracking RTS applications received and disposed off by service in Sindhudurg District, Maharashtra. It supports monitoring of service delivery performance, turnaround and disposal trends, and helps administrators and citizens assess responsiveness under the RTS framework. The reports are published for district-level governance and service delivery oversight, focusing on service-wise application handling within the district.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Grievances"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Daily rainfall data for Sindhudurg District, supporting weather monitoring, hydrological analysis, and local water-resource planning. The catalog enables users to track rainfall variability over time and derive indicators useful for agriculture, disaster preparedness, and climate-related studies at district level. Published as an environment and forest–focused resource, it is intended for researchers, planners, and operational users needing consistent rainfall observations for Sindhudurg District.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Water Quality"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Spatial utility and infrastructure GIS data for Sivaganga Municipality in Tamil Nadu, compiled by municipal administration for urban asset management. The geospatial layers cover streetlights, transformers, manholes, handpumps, borewells, overhead tanks, and key landmarks such as government office buildings, bus stops, culverts, and places of worship. These datasets support planning, maintenance, and service delivery by providing a mapped view of municipal utilities and public infrastructure within the city.",
  "generated_sector": "Governance and Administration; Local Government, Urban; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together size-wise sanction information for the Karnataka State Financial Corporation for the period 2016-2021. It supports analysis of how financial sanctions vary by size categories, enabling trend tracking and comparative assessment across the stated years. The focus on Karnataka makes it suitable for state-level monitoring of lending/sanction patterns and for researchers or policymakers studying banking and finance performance. Published as part of the Finance and Banking domain.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Banking"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides size-wise sanction information for the Financial Year 2021-2022 for the Karnataka State Financial Corporation. It supports analysis of how sanctioned financial support varies by size categories, useful for monitoring lending patterns and assessing distribution across different borrower or project sizes. Published for stakeholders interested in banking and financial assistance trends in Karnataka during 2021-2022.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Banking"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on ongoing projects under the Slum Rehabilitation Authority, Brihanmumbai, supporting planning and monitoring of slum redevelopment initiatives. It focuses on SRA-related redevelopment activities in Brihanmumbai, enabling stakeholders to track project progress and understand the scope of rehabilitation work. The coverage is limited to Brihanmumbai and reflects current, ongoing project status rather than a historical series.",
  "generated_sector": "Housing; Urban Housing"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Small Saving Agency catalog focuses on tracking the number of active small savings (postal savings schemes) agents in Karnataka. It supports monitoring and analysis of agent coverage for schemes such as SAS MPKBY, helping stakeholders assess outreach and operational capacity. The catalog is useful for program management, performance review, and planning related to postal small savings mobilization within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Banking"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together information on Small Savings in Punjab, covering targets, net receipts, and award money received. It supports analysis of collection performance against planned targets and helps track the flow of award-related amounts. These indicators are useful for monitoring financial outcomes of small savings schemes and for administrative review of performance at the state level. The focus is on award, net receipts, and targets for Small Savings.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Banking"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on Social Welfare Officers and old age homes in Tamil Nadu, supporting identification of district-level welfare functionaries and service points. It highlights roles such as District Dowry Prohibition Officer and District Child Marriage Prohibition Officer, alongside facilities for senior care. The collection is useful for governance, monitoring and coordination of social welfare initiatives, and for stakeholders seeking local points of contact within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Haryana Statistical Abstract focuses on social security and social defence, covering police administration, crime-related information, and prison administration. Data are compiled from the Director-General of Police, Haryana and the Director-General of Prisons, Haryana, and include details such as police stations and police posts and the sanctioned strength of the police force in Haryana. The catalog supports analysis of law-and-order capacity and prison administration for planning, monitoring, and research within the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Home Affairs and Enforcement; Police"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Haryana Statistical Abstract on social welfare services compiles information on loans and grants disbursed to eligible persons, including support for Harijan and Scheduled Caste communities, with details by purpose and source. It also tracks progress of key pension schemes in Haryana, such as old age samman allowance, widow pension, disabled pension, and Ladli Social Security Schemes. The catalog supports monitoring of social protection delivery and assessing scheme coverage and performance for policy planning and review.",
  "generated_sector": "Social Development; Women"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Socio Economic Census provides detailed information on the demography and living conditions of households in Sikkim. The collected census data supports evidence-based planning and policy formulation by capturing socio-economic characteristics at the household level. It is useful for identifying development needs, monitoring welfare priorities, and informing targeted interventions within the state. The census approach helps create a structured baseline for governance and social development initiatives.",
  "generated_sector": "Census and Surveys; Census"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog focuses on Solid Waste Management operational gram panchayats under SBMG in Karnataka. It supports planning and monitoring of rural waste management activities at the gram panchayat level, helping track implementation of SBMG-related operations and service delivery. The datasets are useful for local governance, rural development stakeholders, and program managers seeking evidence to improve waste collection, segregation, and related operational processes. The scope is limited to Karnataka.",
  "generated_sector": "Rural; Development"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on solid waste collected and treated in Punjab, covering municipal waste as well as hazardous waste handled through TSDFs. It also includes data on biomedical waste generation and treatment within Punjab. The indicators support monitoring of waste management performance, planning for safe disposal and treatment capacity, and compliance-focused analysis for environmental governance. Data are organized around waste collection and treatment outcomes across relevant waste streams in Punjab.",
  "generated_sector": "Environment and Forest; Sanitation"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The Sports Authority of Karnataka catalog brings together information on grants to state sports associations, supporting development of sports activities and related initiatives. It is intended to help stakeholders understand funding coverage for sports promotion and plan participation, partnerships, and compliance. The scope covers Karnataka, as indicated in the catalog title, and includes grant information for 2021-22.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Youth Affairs"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles information on sports infrastructure facilities available under the Sports Development Authority of Tamil Nadu (SDAT) for 2017-18. It supports planning and monitoring of sports development by mapping the availability of facilities across Tamil Nadu. The focus on sports infrastructure makes it useful for government departments, SDAT stakeholders, and researchers assessing capacity for training, events, and community sports initiatives.",
  "generated_sector": "Youth and Sports; Games"
}

{
  "generated_description": "Startup Hub supports and coordinates innovation and IPR-related activities for technology start-ups across India. Under the Ministry of Electronics and Information Technology (MeitY), it functions as a national facilitation and monitoring center to integrate ecosystem initiatives and promote technology innovation, start-up growth, and creation of intellectual properties. The catalog is intended to help stakeholders access and use information related to MeitY’s start-up ecosystem efforts at the national level.",
  "generated_sector": "Information and Communications; Information and Technology"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles state average agriculture wage information for Karnataka, covering labour engaged in key farm operations such as ploughing, sowing, weeding, reaping and related activities. It also includes wages for work associated with manuring and transplanting, as well as operations linked to livestock grazing and areca and coconut garden activities such as harvesting, peeling and trimming. These wage averages support analysis of agricultural labour costs and planning for policy and program monitoring in the agriculture sector.",
  "generated_sector": "Agriculture; Agricultural Research & Extension"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog compiles Punjab state budget data focused on Capital Account expenditure, covering components such as capital outlay, public debt, and loans and advances from the Central Government. It supports analysis of how capital spending and debt-related flows are allocated over time within the state budget framework. Useful for budget monitoring, fiscal research, and comparative studies of capital financing patterns in Punjab. The data is published under the Finance domain for public access and transparency.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog covers Punjab state budget capital account receipts, detailing inflows from sources such as market loans, loans from SBI and other banks, NABARD and other lenders, and ways and means advances from RBI. It also includes receipts from loans from the Centre, small savings, recoveries of loans and advances, internal state settlement accounts, contingency fund, state provident fund, group insurance fund, reserve funds, deposits and advances suspense, and remittances. These data support budget analysis, fund-flow tracking, and fiscal planning for capital receipts.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog provides Punjab state budget data on Expenditure on Revenue Account, covering major heads such as interest payments, power subsidy, pension and other retirement benefits, police, public works, general education, medical and public health, irrigation and flood control, agricultural and allied activities, road transport, grant-in-aid and contributions, manufacturing and mining, and other expenditure. It supports analysis of how recurring revenue spending is allocated across sectors and helps in budget monitoring, policy review, and fiscal planning for the state.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Revenue"
}

{
  "generated_description": "The catalog brings together state budget data for Punjab on the overall budgetary position, covering receipts and expenditure across revenue and capital accounts. It tracks changes in opening and closing balances, supporting analysis of fiscal performance and budgetary trends. These indicators are useful for government finance monitoring, policy review, and comparative budgeting studies. The focus is on budget components such as revenue, capital, receipts, expenditure, and balance movements for Punjab.",
  "generated_sector": "Finance; Economy"
